Z||000013||Monkeyman||07-29-2001||10:37 PM||||I think my wifes' '98 Cavalier is ugly and ergonomically futzed up, but it's never really had any problems.  We have almost 60k miles on her (combination of city and road miles) and the biggest problem we've ever had was a bad injector at around 50k miles.  Not expensive to replace (dealer did the work).  We didn't even consider extending the factory warranty because it just doesn't seem to be necessary.  That's it other than consumable items such as brakes, oil, etc.  We make occasional trips to southern Ohio (160 miles each way) and have made a trip to northern Wisconsin (800 miles round trip) with no problems whatsoever.  (Well...we had a flat tire once.)  If you can stand the butt ugliness and the crappy ergonomics, buy a Cavalier.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
